{
  "title": "40: al-Ghaafir غافر",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nحٰمٓ‌ ۚ‏(1)\nHAA-MEEM.\nHa. Mim. (H. M.)\nتَنْزِيْلُ الْكِتٰبِ مِنَ اللّٰهِ الْعَزِيْزِ الْعَلِيْمِۙ‏(2)\nTANZEELU KETAABE MENAL LAAHE A’ZEEZIL AL-A’ALEEME.\nThe descent (Revelation) of the Book is from God, the Almighty, All-Knowing,\nغَافِرِ الذَّنْۢبِ وَقَابِلِ التَّوْبِ شَدِيْدِ الْعِقَابِ ذِى الطَّوْلِؕ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَؕ اِلَيْهِ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(3)\nGHAAFERE AZ-ZANBE WAQAABELE AT-TAWBE SHADEEDE E’QAAB ZIL AT-TAWLE LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOO ELAYHE MASEER.\nThe Forgiver of (every) sin, the Accepter of repentance, the Severe to chastise, the Lord of bounty; There is no god but He; unto Him is the ultimate end of the (life) journey (of everything).\nمَا يُجَادِلُ فِىْۤ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ اِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا فَلَا يَغْرُرْكَ تَقَلُّبُهُمْ فِى الْبِلَادِ‏(4)\nMAA YUJAADELU FEE AAYAATIL LAAHE ILLAA LAZEENA KAFAROO FALAA YAGHRURKA TAQALLUBUHUM FIL BELAADE.\nDispute not about the signs of God save those who disbelieve, so (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) let not their going to and from in the cities deceive thee!\nكَذَّبَتْ قَبْلَهُمْ قَوْمُ نُوْحٍ وَّ الْاَحْزَابُ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ وَهَمَّتْ كُلُّ اُمَّةٍۢ بِرَسُوْلِهِمْ لِيَاْخُذُوْهُ ؕ وَجَادَلُوْا بِالْبَاطِلِ لِيُدْحِضُوْا بِهِ الْحَقَّ فَاَخَذْتُهُمْ فَكَيْفَ كَانَ عِقَابِ‏(5)\nKAZZABAT QABLAHUM QAWMO NOOHIN WA YAATIL MIN BA’DEHIM WAHAMMAT KULLO UMMATIN BERASOOLEHEM LEEAKHUZOOHU WAJAADALOOA BIL-BAATELE LEEDHEZOOA BEHIL HAQQA FAAKHAZTUHUM FA-KAYFA KAANA E’EQAABE.\nDid belie the people of Noah before them and the parties after them, and did scheme every people against their apostle that they may seize him and they disputed by the falsehood that they might by it render into naught the truth, so I did seize them; and how (terrible) was then My retribution?\nوَكَذٰلِكَ حَقَّتْ كَلِمَتُ رَبِّكَ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اَنَّهُمْ اَصْحٰبُ النَّارِ ؔ‌ۘ‏(6)\nWA KAZAALEKA HAQQAT KALEMATU RABBEKA A’LAL LAZEENA KAFAROO ANNAHUM ASHAABUN NAAR.\nAnd thus did prove true the sentence of thy Lord against those who did disbelieve that they are the inmates of the fire.\nاَلَّذِيْنَ يَحْمِلُوْنَ الْعَرْشَ وَمَنْ حَوْلَهٗ يُسَبِّحُوْنَ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّهِمْ وَيُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِهٖ وَيَسْتَغْفِرُوْنَ لِلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا‌ ۚ رَبَّنَا وَسِعْتَ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ رَّحْمَةً وَّعِلْمًا فَاغْفِرْ لِلَّذِيْنَ تَابُوْا وَاتَّبَعُوْا سَبِيْلَكَ وَقِهِمْ عَذَابَ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(7)\nLAZEENA YAHMELOONA AL-A’ARSHA WA MAN HAWLAHU YUSABBEHOONA BE-HAMDE RABBEHIM WA YOAMENOONA BEHI WAYASTAGHFEROONA LILLAZEENA AAMANOO RABBANAA WASEA’TA KULLA SHAY-IN RAHMATAM WA I’LMAA FAGH-FIR LILLAZEENA TAABOO WAT TABA-O’O SABEELAKA WAQEHEM A’ZAABAL JAHEEM.\nThose who bear the ‘Arsh’ and those around it celebrate the praise of their Lord and believe in Him and seek forgiveness for those who believe in Him (saying): “O’ Our Lord! Thou comprehendeth all things in (Thy) mercy and knowledge, therefore forgive Thou those who turn (unto Thee) and follow Thy way, and save them from the torment of the Hell:\nرَبَّنَا وَاَدْخِلْهُمْ جَنّٰتِ عَدْنِ اۨلَّتِىْ وَعَدْتَّهُمْ وَمَنْ صَلَحَ مِنْ اٰبَآئِهِمْ وَاَزْوَاجِهِمْ وَذُرِّيّٰتِهِمْ ؕ اِنَّكَ اَنْتَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ ۙ‏(8)\nRABBANAA WAADKHELHUM JANNATIN A’ADNE LATEE WAA’ADTTAHUM WA MAN SALAHA MIN AAABAAEHEM WA AZWAAJEHIM WAZURREETEHEM INNAKA ANTA A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nO’ Our Lord! Admit them into the ever-blissful gardens which Thou hast promised unto them and those who do good from their fathers, and, their wives, and their children; for Thou art the Almighty, the All-Wise!\nوَقِهِمُ السَّيِّاٰتِ ؕ وَمَنْ تَقِ السَّيِّاٰتِ يَوْمَئِذٍ فَقَدْ رَحِمْتَهٗ ؕ وَذٰ لِكَ هُوَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(9)\nWAQEHEMU SAYYE-AATE WA MAN TAQE SAYYE-AATE YAWMA-EZIN FAQAD RAHEMTAH WAZAA LEKA HOWA FAWZUL A’ZEEM.\nAnd keep them from evil: and whomsoever keepest thou from evil, this day indeed Thou hast bestowed mercy on him, and that, it is a Mighty Achievement.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا يُنَادَوْنَ لَمَقْتُ اللّٰهِ اَكْبَرُ مِنْ مَّقْتِكُمْ اَنْفُسَكُمْ اِذْ تُدْعَوْنَ اِلَى الْاِيْمَانِ فَتَكْفُرُوْنَ‏(10)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO YONAADAWNA LAMAQTU LAAHE AKBARO MIN MMAQTEKUM ANFOSAKUM IZ TUDA’AWNA ELAL AL-AEEMAANE FA TAKFOROONA.\nVerily, those who disbelieve, unto them shall a voice cry: “Certainly, God’s hatred (of you) is greater than your hatred of yourselves when ye were called upon unto the faith and ye did disbelieve!\nقَالُوْا رَبَّنَاۤ اَمَتَّنَا اثْنَتَيْنِ وَاَحْيَيْتَنَا اثْنَتَيْنِ فَاعْتَرَفْنَا بِذُنُوْبِنَا فَهَلْ اِلٰى خُرُوْجٍ مِّنْ سَبِيْلٍ‏(11)\nQAALOO RABBANAA AAMATTANAA ASNATAYNE WAAHYAYTANAA ASNATAYNE FAAA’TARAFNAA BEZUNOOBENAA FA HAL ELAA KHUROOJIN MIN SABEELIN.\nThey shall say: “O’ our Lord! Twice didst thou cause us to die, and twice didst Thou give us life, and (now) we do confess our sins: Is there then a way to get out (of this)?\nذٰ لِكُمْ بِاَنَّهٗۤ اِذَا دُعِىَ اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ كَفَرْتُمْ ۚ وَاِنْ يُّشْرَكْ بِهٖ تُؤْمِنُوْا ؕ فَالْحُكْمُ لِلّٰهِ الْعَلِىِّ الْكَبِيْرِ‏(12)\nZAA ZAALEKUM BE-ANNAHU EZAA DUE’EAAA LAAHO WAHDAH KAFARTUM WA YYUSHRAK BEHI LAM TOAMENOO FA HUKMO LILLAAHE AL-A’ALEAAAE AL-KABEERE.\nThis (hath befallen you) for when God alone was called upon, ye did disbelieve, and when associates were assigned unto Him, ye believed; And (all) authority is God’s, the Highest, the Greatest.\nهُوَ الَّذِىْ يُرِيْكُمْ اٰيٰتِهٖ وَيُنَزِّلُ لَكُمْ مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ رِزْقًا ؕ وَمَا يَتَذَكَّرُ اِلَّا مَنْ يُّنِيْبُ‏(13)\nHOWA LAZEE YUREEKUM AAYAATEHI WAYUNAZZELU LAKUM MENAL SAMAAA-E RIZQAN WA MAA YATAZAKKARU ILLAA MAN YYUNEEBU.\nHe it is Who showeth you His signs and sendeth down for you from the heaven - sustenance; but payeth not heed save he who turneth (unto Him).\nفَادْعُوا اللّٰهَ مُخْلِصِيْنَ لَهُ الدِّيْنَ وَلَوْ كَرِهَ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ‏(14)\nFAADU’OOA LAAHA MUKHLESEENA LAHUL DEENA WA LAW KAREHA KAAFEROON.\nSo call ye upon God, devoting religion exclusively unto Him, though averse be the dis believers.\nرَفِيْعُ الدَّرَجٰتِ ذُو الْعَرْشِ‌ ۚ يُلْقِى الرُّوْحَ مِنْ اَمْرِهٖ عَلٰى مَنْ يَّشَآءُ مِنْ عِبَادِهٖ لِيُنْذِرَ يَوْمَ التَّلَاقِ ۙ‏(15)\nRAFEEU’U AD-DARAJAATE ZUL A’RSHIL YULQEAA AR-ROOHA MIN AMREHI A’LAA MAN YASHAAA-O MIN E’BAADEHI LEENZERA YAWMA AT-TALAAQE.\nThe Exalter of the ranks, the Lord of ‘Arsh’ (the Supreme Authority); Causeth forth He the spirit at His own behest on whomsoever He willeth of His servants, that he may warn (men) of the day of meeting,\nيَوْمَ هُمْ بَارِزُوْنَ ۚ لَا يَخْفٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ مِنْهُمْ شَىْءٌ ؕ لِمَنِ الْمُلْكُ الْيَوْمَ ؕ لِلّٰهِ الْوَاحِدِ الْقَهَّارِ‏(16)\nYAWMA HUM BAAREZOONA LAA YAKHFAA A’LAL LAAHE MINHUM SHAY-UN LEMANIT A’LAYNAA YAWMA LILLAAHE AL-WAAHEDE AL-QAHHAARE.\n(Of) the Day when they shall come forth (from their graves), when naught about them shall be hidden from God. (A voice shall ask): “Whose is the kingdom this day? (It is) God’s, the One, the Subduer (absolute)!\nاَ لْيَوْمَ تُجْزٰى كُلُّ نَفْسٍۢ بِمَا كَسَبَتْ ؕ لَا ظُلْمَ الْيَوْمَ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ سَرِيْعُ الْحِسَابِ‏(17)\nA’ZAABAN LYAWMA TUJZAA KULLO NAFSIM BEMAA KASABAT LAA ZULMA YAWMA INNAL LAAHA SAREE-U’L HESAAB.\nThis day shall every soul be recompensed for what it hath earned; No injustice (shall be done on the Day); Verily God is quick in reckoning.\nوَاَنْذِرْهُمْ يَوْمَ الْاٰزِفَةِ اِذِ الْقُلُوْبُ لَدَى الْحَنَاجِرِ كٰظِمِيْنَ ؕ مَا لِلظّٰلِمِيْنَ مِنْ حَمِيْمٍ وَّلَا شَفِيْعٍ يُّطَاعُ ؕ‏(18)\nWAANZERHUM YAWMA AL-AAAZEFATE EZIM BALAGHATIL LADAA AL-HANAAJERE KAAZEMEENA MAA LIZ-ZAALEMEENA MIN HAMEEMIN WA LAA SHAFEEA’IN YYUTAAU’U.\nAnd (thou) warn them, then, of the approaching Day, when (men’s) hearts shall rise up to their throats choking; For the unjust there shall not be any sincere friend nor an intercessor who shall prevail.\nيَعْلَمُ خَآئِنَةَ الْاَعْيُنِ وَمَا تُخْفِى الصُّدُوْرُ‏(19)\nYA’LAMO KHAAENATA AL-AAA’YUNE WA MAA TUKHFEAA AS-SUDOORU.\nHe knoweth the deceit of the eye, and what the breasts conceal.\nوَاللّٰهُ يَقْضِىْ بِالْحَقِّؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ يَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖ لَا يَقْضُوْنَ بِشَىْءٍؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْبَصِيْرُ‏(20)\nWAL LAAHO YAQZEE BIL-HAQ WAL LAZEENA YAD-O’ONA MIN DOONEHI LAA YAQZOONA BE-SHAYIN INNAL LAAHA HOWA SAMEE-U’L AL-BASEERU.\nAnd God judgeth with truth; and those whom they call upon besides Him can judge not any thing; Verily God is the All-Hearing, the All-Seeing.\nاَوَلَمْ يَسِيْرُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ فَيَنْظُرُوْا كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الَّذِيْنَ كَانُوْا مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْؕ كَانُوْا هُمْ اَشَدَّ مِنْهُمْ قُوَّةً وَّاٰثَارًا فِى الْاَرْضِ فَاَخَذَهُمُ اللّٰهُ بِذُنُوْبِهِمْؕ وَمَا كَانَ لَهُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ مِنْ وَّاقٍ‏(21)\nAWALAM YASEEROO FIL ARZE FAYANZOROO KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL LAZEENA KAANOO MIN QABLEHIM KAANOO HUM ASHADDA MINHUM QUWWAH WWAASAARAN FIL ARZE TOOFAANO LAAHO BEZUNOOBEHEM WA MAA KAANA LAHUM MENAL LAAHE MIN WWAAQIN.\nWhat! Have not they travelled in the earth and seen how (destructive) hath been the end of those who were before them? (though) They were mightier in strength than these and in their relics in the earth, but God seized them (with destruction) for their sins; and there was not for them any shelter against (the wrath of) God.\nذٰلِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ كَانَتْ تَّاْتِيْهِمْ رُسُلُهُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ فَكَفَرُوْا فَاَخَذَهُمُ اللّٰهُؕ اِنَّهٗ قَوِىٌّ شَدِيْدُ الْعِقَابِ‏(22)\nZAALEKA BE-ANNAHUM KAANAT TTAATEEHEM JAAA-ATHUM BIL-BAYYENAATE FA KAFAROO TOOFAANO LAAH INNAHU QAWEAAAUN SHADEEDUL E’QAAB.\nThis, because there hath come unto them their apostles with clear proofs, but they disbelieved, so did seize them God; Verily He is All-Strong, Vehement in retribution.\nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا مُوْسٰى بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَسُلْطٰنٍ مُّبِيْنٍۙ‏(23)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA MOOSAA BE-AAYAATENAA WASULTAANIN MOBEEN.\nAnd indeed sent We Moses with Our signs and a clear authority\nاِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ وَ هَامٰنَ وَقَارُوْنَ فَقَالُوْا سٰحِرٌ كَذَّابٌ‏(24)\nELAA FIR-A’WNA WA HAAMAANA WA QAAROONA FA-QAALOO SAAHERUN KAZZAABUN.\nUnto Pharaoh and Haman and Qarun, but they said: “(This is a) great lying sorcerer!\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَهُمْ بِالْحَقِّ مِنْ عِنْدِنَا قَالُوْا اقْتُلُوْۤا اَبْنَآءَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مَعَهٗ وَاسْتَحْيُوْا نِسَآءَهُمْؕ وَمَا كَيْدُ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ اِلَّا فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ‏(25)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-AHUM BIL-HAQQE MIN I’NDENAA QAALOO AQTULOOA AABNAAA LAZEENA AAMANOO MA-A’HU WAASTAHYOOA NESAAAHUM WA MAA KAYDU KAAFEREEN ILLAA FEE ZALAALIM.\nAnd he brought unto them the truth from unto Us, said they: “Slay ye the sons of those who believe with him and leave their women alive;” but the plot of the disbelievers is nothing but a failure.\nوَقَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ ذَرُوْنِىْۤ اَقْتُلْ مُوْسٰى وَلْيَدْعُ رَبَّهٗ‌ۚ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ اَنْ يُّبَدِّلَ دِيْنَكُمْ اَوْ اَنْ يُّظْهِرَ فِى الْاَرْضِ الْفَسَادَ‏(26)\nWA QAALA FIRA’WNO ZAROONEAA AAQTUL MOOSAA WALYADU’U WAL INNEE AKHAAFO AN YYUBADDELA DEENAKUM AW AN YYUZHERA FIL ARZE FASAADA.\nAnd said Pharaoh: “Let me alone I will slay Moses, and let him call upon his Lord; Verily I fear that he may change your religion, or he may cause mischief to appear in the land.\nوَقَالَ مُوْسٰٓى اِنِّىْ عُذْتُ بِرَبِّىْ وَرَبِّكُمْ مِّنْ كُلِّ مُتَكَبِّرٍ لَّا يُؤْمِنُ بِيَوْمِ الْحِسَابِ‏(27)\nWA QAALA MOOSAA INNEE U’ZTO BE-RABBEE WA RABBEKUM MIN KULLE MUTAKABBERIN LAA BIL LAAHE BE-YAWMID HESAAB.\nAnd Moses said: “Verily, I take refuge with my Lord and your Lord from every arrogant one who believeth not in the Day of Reckoning!\nوَقَالَ رَجُلٌ مُّؤْمِنٌ ‌ۖ مِّنْ اٰلِ فِرْعَوْنَ يَكْتُمُ اِيْمَانَهٗۤ اَتَقْتُلُوْنَ رَجُلًا اَنْ يَّقُوْلَ رَبِّىَ اللّٰهُ وَقَدْ جَآءَكُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ مِنْ رَّبِّكُمْ ؕ وَاِنْ يَّكُ كَاذِبًا فَعَلَيْهِ كَذِبُهٗ ؕ وَاِنْ يَّكُ صَادِقًا يُّصِبْكُمْ بَعْضُ الَّذِىْ يَعِدُكُمْ ۚ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَهْدِىْ مَنْ هُوَ مُسْرِفٌ كَذَّابٌ‏(28)\nWA QAALA RAJOLUM MOAMENUN MIN AALE FIR-A’WNA YAKTUMU AEEMAANAH AATAQTULOONA RAJULAN AN YAQOOLA RABBEYAL LAAHO WA QAD JAAA-AKUM BIL-BAYYENAATE MIN RABBEKUM WA YYAKU KAAZEBAN FA-A’LAYHE KAZEBUH WA YYAKU SAADEQAN YYUSEBKUM BA’ZUL LAZEE YA-E’DOKUM INNAL LAAHA LAA YAHDEE MAN HOWA MUSREFUN KAZZAABUN.\nAnd said a man who was a Believer, from among the people of Pharaoh: who used to conceal his faith: “What! slay ye a man for sayeth he ‘My Lord is God,’ and indeed he hath brought unto you clear proofs (of his mission) from your Lord? While if he be a liar, on him will be his lie, and if he be truthful, then will afflict you some of what he warneth you (with); Verily, God guideth not him who is extravagant (and) a liar\nيٰقَوْمِ لَكُمُ الْمُلْكُ الْيَوْمَ ظٰهِرِيْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ فَمَنْ يَّنْصُرُنَا مِنْۢ بَاْسِ اللّٰهِ اِنْ جَآءَنَا ؕ قَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ مَاۤ اُرِيْكُمْ اِلَّا مَاۤ اَرٰى وَمَاۤ اَهْدِيْكُمْ اِلَّا سَبِيْلَ الرَّشَادِ‏(29)\nLE-QAWMEHI LAKOMUL A’LAYNAA YAWMA ZAAHEREENA FIL ARZE FAMAN YYANSURUNAA MIN BAASE LAAHE IN JAAA-ANAA QAALA FIRA’WNO MAA AUREEKUM ILLAA MAA AARAA WA MAA AAHDEEKUM ILLAA SABEELA AR-RASHAADE.\nO’ my people! Yours is the kingdom this day, being prevailing in the land, but who will help us against the wrath of God if it cometh upon us?” Pharaoh said: “I show you not aught but what I (myself) see, and I guide you not but in a right way.\nوَقَالَ الَّذِىْۤ اٰمَنَ يٰقَوْمِ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ مِّثْلَ يَوْمِ الْاَحْزَابِۙ‏(30)\nWA QAALA LAZEE AAMANA LE-QAWMEHI INNEE AKHAAFO A’LAYKUM MISLA YAWMIL AL-AAHZAABE.\nAnd said he who believed: “O’ my people! verily, I fear, (that it may fall) on you the like of that (what befell) the parties,\nمِثْلَ دَاْبِ قَوْمِ نُوْحٍ وَّعَادٍ وَّثَمُوْدَ وَالَّذِيْنَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْؕ وَمَا اللّٰهُ يُرِيْدُ ظُلْمًا لِّلْعِبَادِ‏(31)\nMISLA DAABE QAWME NOOHIN WWAA’AADIN WA WAL LAZEENA MIN BAA’DEHEM WA MAA LAAHO YOREEDO ZULMAWN LLELE’EBAADE.\nThe like of that (what befell) the people of Noah and ’Ad and Thamud and those (who came) after them; and God intendeth not injustice unto (His) servants\nوَيٰقَوْمِ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ يَوْمَ التَّنَادِۙ‏(32)\nWA LE-QAWMEHI INNEE AKHAAFO A’LAYKUM YAWMA AT-TANAADE.\nAnd O’ my people! I fear for you the Day of Calling out (each other)\nيَوْمَ تُوَلُّوْنَ مُدْبِرِيْنَ‌ۚ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ مِنْ عَاصِمٍۚ وَمَنْ يُّضْلِلِ اللّٰهُ فَمَا لَهٗ مِنْ هَادٍ‏(33)\nYAWMA TOOLLOONA MUDBEREEN MAA LAKUM MENAL LAAHE MIN A’AASEMIN WA MAN YYUZLELE LAAHO FAMAA LAHU MIN HAADIN.\nThe Day on which ye shall be turned back (from the Judgment unto the Hell), (when) for you there shall not be any saviour from (the wrath of) God; and whomsoever God alloweth to stray, for him shall not be any guide,\nوَلَقَدْ جَآءَكُمْ يُوْسُفُ مِنْ قَبْلُ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ فَمَا زِلْتُمْ فِىْ شَكٍّ مِّمَّا جَآءَكُمْ بِهٖ ؕ حَتّٰٓى اِذَا هَلَكَ قُلْتُمْ لَنْ يَّبْعَثَ اللّٰهُ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهٖ رَسُوْلًا ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يُضِلُّ اللّٰهُ مَنْ هُوَ مُسْرِفٌ مُّرْتَابٌ  ۚ ۖ‏(34)\nWA LAQAD JAAA-AKUM YOOSUFU MIN QABLO BIL-BAYYENAATE FAMAA ZELTUM FEE SHAKKIM MIMMAA JAAA-AKUM BEHI HATTAA EZAA HALAKA IZ QULTUM LAN YYABA’ASA LAAHO MIN BA’DEHI RASOOLAM KAZAALEKA YOZILLO LAAHO MAN HOWA MUSREFUN MMURTAABUN.\nAnd indeed came unto you Yusuf before, with clear proofs (of his mission), but ye ever doubted about what he brought; until when he died ye said: ‘Never will God raise any apostle after him;’ Thus doth God allow him to stray, who is an extravagant, a doubter.\nاۨلَّذِيْنَ يُجَادِلُوْنَ فِىْۤ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ بِغَيْرِ سُلْطٰنٍ اَتٰٮهُمْ ؕ كَبُرَ مَقْتًا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ وَعِنْدَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يَطْبَعُ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ قَلْبِ مُتَكَبِّرٍ جَبَّارٍ‏(35)\nLAZEENA YUJAADELOONA FEE AAYAATIL LAAHE BEGHAYRIL SULTAANIN ATAAHUM KABURA MAQTAN I’NDAL LAAHE WA I’NDAL LAZEENA AAMANOO KAZAALEKA YATBA-U’L LAAHO A’LAA KULLE QALBE MUTAKABBERIN JABBAARIN.\nThose who dispute about the Signs of God without any authority having come unto them; are greatly hated by God and by those who believe; Thus God setteth a seal over every heart which is arrogant and haughty.\nوَقَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ يٰهَامٰنُ ابْنِ لِىْ صَرْحًا لَّعَلِّىْۤ اَبْلُغُ الْاَسْبَابَۙ‏(36)\nWA QAALA FIRA’WNO YAAHAAMAANO MARYAM LEE SARHAL LA-A’LLEE AABLUGHU AL-AASBAABA.\nAnd said Pharaoh: “O’ Haman! Build thou for me a tower that I may reach the means of access,\nاَسْبَابَ السَّمٰوٰتِ فَاَطَّلِعَ اِلٰٓى اِلٰهِ مُوْسٰى وَاِنِّىْ لَاَظُنُّهٗ كَاذِبًا ؕ وَكَذٰلِكَ زُيِّنَ لِفِرْعَوْنَ سُوْٓءُ عَمَلِهٖ وَصُدَّ عَنِ السَّبِيْلِ ؕ وَمَا كَيْدُ فِرْعَوْنَ اِلَّا فِىْ تَبَابٍ‏(37)\nAASBAABA SAMAAWAATE FAATTALEA’A ELAA ELAAHE MOOSAA WA INNEE LA-AZUNNOHU KAAZEBAN WA KAZAALEKA ZUYYENA LE-FIR-A’WNA SOOO-UL A’AMALEH WASUDDA A’NIL SABEELE WA MAA KAYDU FIR-A’WNA ILLAA FEE TABAABIN.\nThe means of access unto heavens, so that I (may) mount up to reach unto God of Moses, and verily I think him to be a liar;” and thus was made fair-seeming unto Pharaoh the evil of his deed and he was turned away from the (right) way; and the plot of Pharaoh was not but (to end) into (his own) ruin.\nوَقَالَ الَّذِىْۤ اٰمَنَ يٰقَوْمِ اتَّبِعُوْنِ اَهْدِكُمْ سَبِيْلَ الرَّشَادِ‌ۚ‏(38)\nWA QAALA LAZEE AAMANA LE-QAWMEHI ATTABEU’OONE AAHDEKUM SABEELA AR-RASHAADE.\nAnd said he who hath believed: “O’ my people! follow me, I will show you the way to the right guidance\nيٰقَوْمِ اِنَّمَا هٰذِهِ الْحَيٰوةُ الدُّنْيَا مَتَاعٌ وَّاِنَّ الْاٰخِرَةَ هِىَ دَارُ الْقَرَارِ‏(39)\nLE-QAWMEHI INNAMAA HAAZEHE HAYAATUD DUNYAA LIL-MOTAALLAQAATE WWAANNA AAKHERATA HEYA DAARU AL-QARAARE.\nO’ my people! the life of this world is only (a passing ) enjoyment, and verily, the hereafter is the abode to last.\nمَنْ عَمِلَ سَيِّئَةً فَلَا يُجْزٰٓى اِلَّا مِثْلَهَا ۚ وَمَنْ عَمِلَ صَالِحًا مِّنْ ذَكَرٍ اَوْ اُنْثٰى وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ يَدْخُلُوْنَ الْجَنَّةَ يُرْزَقُوْنَ فِيْهَا بِغَيْرِ حِسَابٍ‏(40)\nMAN A’MELA SAYYE-ATANW FALAA YUJZAAA ILLAA MESLAHAA WA MAN A’MELA SAALEHAN MIN ZAKARIN AW UNSAA WA HOWA MUMENUN FA-OOLAAA-EKA YADKHOLOONA JANNATA YURZAQOONA FEEHAA BEGHAYRIL HESAAB.\nWhosoever shall have wrought an evil shall not be recompensed but the like of it, and whosoever shall have wrought good, whether a male or a female, and he be a believer, these shall enter the Garden, wherein they shall be provided with sustenance with out measure.\nوَيٰقَوْمِ مَا لِىْۤ اَدْعُوْكُمْ اِلَى النَّجٰوةِ وَتَدْعُوْنَنِىْۤ اِلَى النَّارِؕ‏(41)\nWA LE-QAWMEHI MAA LEE AADU’OOKUM ELAL AN-NAJAAWTE WATADU’OONANEAA ELAL NAAR.\nO’ my people! how is it that I invite you unto salvation and ye call me unto fire?\nتَدْعُوْنَنِىْ لِاَكْفُرَ بِاللّٰهِ وَاُشْرِكَ بِهٖ مَا لَيْسَ لِىْ بِهٖ عِلْمٌ وَّاَنَا اَدْعُوْكُمْ اِلَى الْعَزِيْزِ الْغَفَّارِ‏(42)\nTADU’OONANEAA LEAAKFURA BIL-LAAHE WAASHREKA BEHI MAA LAYSA LEE BEHI I’LMUM WWAANAA AADU’OOKUM ELAL A’ZEEZIL AL-GHAFFAARE.\nYe call on me that I should disbelieve in God and associate with Him that I have no knowledge of, and I invite you unto the Almighty, and the Oft-Forgiving (Lord)\nلَا جَرَمَ اَنَّمَا تَدْعُوْنَنِىْۤ اِلَيْهِ لَيْسَ لَهٗ دَعْوَةٌ فِى الدُّنْيَا وَلَا فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ وَاَنَّ مَرَدَّنَاۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِ وَاَنَّ الْمُسْرِفِيْنَ هُمْ اَصْحٰبُ النَّارِ‏(43)\nLAA JARAMA ANNAMAA TADU’OONANEAA ELAYHE LAYSA LAHU DAA’WATUN FIL DUNYAA WA LAA FIL AAKHERATE WA ANNAL MARADDANAA ELAL LAAHE WA ANNAL MUSREFEEN HUM ASHAABUN NAAR.\nNo doubt is there that what ye call me unto, hath no right to be invoked in this world nor in the hereafter, and our return is unto God, and that the extravagants shall be the inmates of the (Hell) fire.\nفَسَتَذْكُرُوْنَ مَاۤ اَقُوْلُ لَكُمْؕ وَاُفَوِّضُ اَمْرِىْۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ بَصِيْرٌۢ بِالْعِبَادِ‏(44)\nFASATAZKUROONA MAA AAQOOLU LAKUM WAAFAWZU AMREE ELAL LAAH INNAL LAAHA BASEER BIL-E'BAAD.\nAnd ye shall remember what I say unto you, and I entrust my affair unto God: verily, God seeth well (His) servants\nفَوَقٰٮهُ اللّٰهُ سَيِّاٰتِ مَا مَكَرُوْا وَحَاقَ بِاٰلِ فِرْعَوْنَ سُوْٓءُ الْعَذَابِ‌ۚ‏(45)\nFAWAQAAHU LAAHO SAYAAATE MAA MAKAROOA WAHAAQA BE-AALE FIR-A’WNA SOOO-UL A’ZAABE.\nAnd God preserved him from the evils of what they planned; and the woe of the chastisement encompassed the people of Pharaoh.\nاَلنَّارُ يُعْرَضُوْنَ عَلَيْهَا غُدُوًّا وَّعَشِيًّا ۚ وَيَوْمَ تَقُوْمُ السَّاعَةُ اَدْخِلُوْۤا اٰلَ فِرْعَوْنَ اَشَدَّ الْعَذَابِ‏(46)\nAALNNAARU YUA’RAZOONA A’LAYHAA GHUDOOA WWAA’ASHEEA WA YAWMA YAQOOMUS SAA-A’TO AADKHELOOA AALA FIR-A’WNA ASHADDA A’ZAABE.\nThe fire: they shall be exposed unto it (every) morning and evening and on the Day when shall be established the ‘Hour (of Reckoning)’ (the sentence shall be) “Admit ye the people of Pharaoh to the severest of the chastisement.\nوَاِذْ يَتَحَآجُّوْنَ فِى النَّارِ فَيَقُوْلُ الضُّعَفٰٓؤُا لِلَّذِيْنَ اسْتَكْبَرُوْۤا اِنَّا كُنَّا لَكُمْ تَبَعًا فَهَلْ اَنْتُمْ مُّغْنُوْنَ عَنَّا نَصِيْبًا مِّنَ النَّارِ‏(47)\nWA IZ YATAHAAJJOONA FIL NAAR FAYAQOOLO AZ-ZUA’AFAAAUA LILLAZEENA ASTAKBAROOA INNAA KUNNAA LAKUM TABAA’AN FA HAL ANTUM MMUGHNOONA WAGH NASEEBAN MENAL NAAR.\nAnd when they shall wrangle together in the fire, then shall say the weak unto those who were arrogant: “Verily we were unto you the followers; will ye then relieve us from something of the fire?\nقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ اسْتَكْبَرُوْۤا اِنَّا كُلٌّ فِيْهَاۤۙاِنَّ اللّٰهَ قَدْ حَكَمَ بَيْنَ الْعِبَادِ‏(48)\nQAALA LAZEENA ASTAKBAROOA INNAA KULLUL FEEHAAAENNA LAAHA QAD HAKAMA BAYNA A’LAL.\nShall say those who were arrogant: “Verily, we are all in it; Verily, God hath indeed judged between (His) servants,\nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ فِى النَّارِ لِخَزَنَةِ جَهَنَّمَ ادْعُوْا رَبَّكُمْ يُخَفِّفْ عَنَّا يَوْمًا مِّنَ الْعَذَابِ‏(49)\nWA QAALA LAZEENA FIL NAAR LEKHAZANATE JAHANNAMA O’O TAQUL YUKHAFFEF WAGH YAWMAN MENAL A’ZAABE.\nAnd shall say those in the fire unto the guards of hell: “Call ye upon your Lord that He may lighten unto us (at least for) a day, of the chastisement.\nقَالُوْۤا اَوَلَمْ تَكُ تَاْتِيْكُمْ رُسُلُكُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ ؕ قَالُوْا بَلٰى ؕ قَالُوْا‌ فَادْعُوْا ۚ وَمَا دُعٰٓؤُا الْكٰفِرِيْنَ اِلَّا فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ‏(50)\nQAALOO AWALAM TAKU TAATEEKUM RUSULUKUM BIL-BAYYENAATE QAALOO BALAA QAALOO FA O’O WA MAA DUA’AAAUA KAAFEREEN ILLAA FEE ZALAALIM.\nThey shall say: “Came not unto you your apostles with clear proofs (of their mission)? They shall say: “Yea!” They shall say: “(why not yourselves) Cry ye then (for help)?” but the cry of the disbelievers shall not be but in vain.\nاِنَّا لَنَنْصُرُ رُسُلَنَا وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا وَيَوْمَ يَقُوْمُ الْاَشْهَادُ ۙ‏(51)\nINNAA LANANSURU RUSULANAA WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA WA YAWMA YAQOOMUL AL-AASHHAADU.\nVerily, We do help Our apostles, and those who believe, in the life of this world and on the day when shall stand forth the witnesses,\nيَوْمَ لَا يَنْفَعُ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ مَعْذِرَتُهُمْ وَلَهُمُ اللَّعْنَةُ وَلَهُمْ سُوْٓءُ الدَّارِ‏(52)\nYAWMA LAA YANFAU’N ZAALEMEEN MA’ZERATOHUM WA LAHOMUL AL-LAA’NATU WA LAHUM SOOO-UL AD-DAARE.\nThe day when shall benefit not the unjust their excuses, and for them shall be the curse, and for them shall be the evil abode (in Hell).\nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا مُوْسَى الْهُدٰى وَاَوْرَثْنَا بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ الْكِتٰبَۙ‏(53)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA MOOSAL HODAA WAAWRASNAA BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ KETAABA.\nAnd indeed We gave Moses the guidance, and We made the children of Israel inherit the Book,\nهُدًى وَّذِكْرٰى لِاُولِى الْاَلْبَابِ‏(54)\nHODAM WA ZIKRAA LE-ULIL ULIL ALBAABE.\nA guidance and a reminder unto the men endued with understanding.\nفَاصْبِرْ اِنَّ وَعْدَ اللّٰهِ حَقٌّ وَّاسْتَغْفِرْ لِذَنْۢبِكَ وَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ بِالْعَشِىِّ وَالْاِبْكَارِ‏(55)\nFAS-BIR INNAL WA’DAL LAAHE HAQQUWN WWAASTAGHFER LE-ZAMBEKA WASABBEH BE-HAMDE RABBEKA BIL-A’ASHEAAAE WAL AEBKAARE.\nSo be thou patient; verily, the promise of God is true; and seek protection for thy (followers’) shortcomings, and celebrate the praise of thy Lord in the evening and the morning.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يُجَادِلُوْنَ فِىْۤ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ بِغَيْرِ سُلْطٰنٍ اَتٰٮهُمْۙ اِنْ فِىْ صُدُوْرِهِمْ اِلَّا كِبْرٌ مَّا هُمْ بِبَالِغِيْهِؕ فَاسْتَعِذْ بِاللّٰهِؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْبَصِيْرُ‏(56)\nINNAL LAZEENA YUJAADELOONA FEE AAYAATIL LAAHE BEGHAYRIL SULTAANIN ATAAHUM IN FEE SODOOREHIM ILLAA KEBRUN MAA HUM BEBAALEGHEEHE FAS-TA-I’Z BILLAAH INNAHU HOWA SAMEE-U’L AL-BASEERU.\nVerily, those who dispute about the signs of God without any authority having come unto them, naught is there in their breast but (a vain desire ) to become great, which they shall attain not; therefore seek (thou) refuge in God, verily He is the All Hearing, the All-Seeing.\nلَخَلْقُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ اَكْبَرُ مِنْ خَلْقِ النَّاسِ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(57)\nLAKHALQU SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE AKBARO MIN KHALQIS NAASE LAAKINNAL AKSARAN NAASE LAA YA’LAMOON.\nSurely, the creation of the heavens and the earth is greater than the creation of the people, but most people know not.\nوَمَا يَسْتَوِى الْاَعْمٰى وَالْبَصِيْرُ ۙ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَ عَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ وَلَا الْمُسِىْٓءُ ؕ قَلِيْلًا مَّا تَتَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(58)\nWA MAA YASTAWEAA A-A’MAA WAL BASEERU WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE WA LAA AL-MUSEAAAAU QALEELAA MAA TATAZAKKAROONA.\nNot equal are the blind and the seeing, nor those who believe and do good and the doers of evil (are equal); little is it that ye reflect.\nاِنَّ السَّاعَةَ لَاٰتِيَةٌ لَّا رَيْبَ فِيْهَا وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(59)\nINNAL SAA-A’TA LAATEETUN LAA RAYBA FEEHAA LAAKINNAL AKSARAN NAASE LAA YOAMENOONA.\nVerily, the Hour (of Reckoning) is to come, there is no doubt therein, but most people believe not.\nوَقَالَ رَبُّكُمُ ادْعُوْنِىْۤ اَسْتَجِبْ لَكُمْؕ اِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يَسْتَكْبِرُوْنَ عَنْ عِبَادَتِىْ سَيَدْخُلُوْنَ جَهَنَّمَ دَاخِرِيْنَ‏(60)\nWA QAALA RABBUKUMU ADU’OONEAA AASTAJEB LAKUM INNAL LAZEENA YASTAKBEROONA A’N E’EBAADATEAA SA-YADKHOLOONA JAHANNAMA DAAKHEREENA.\nAnd sayeth your Lord: “Call ye unto Me, I will answer you;” Verily those who are arrogant to serve Me, shall soon enter Hell, disgraced.\nاَللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ الَّيْلَ لِتَسْكُنُوْا فِيْهِ وَالنَّهَارَ مُبْصِرًا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَذُوْ فَضْلٍ عَلَى النَّاسِ وَ لٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(61)\nALLAAHO LAZEE JA-A’LA LAKOMUL LAYLA LETASKONOO FEEHE WAN NAHAARA MUBSERAN INNAL LAAHA LAZOO FAZLIN A’LAL NAASE WA LAAKENNA AKSARAN NAASE LAA YASHKOROON.\nGod is He who hath made for you the night that ye may rest in it and the day to give you light; Verily God is gracious unto the people, but most people thank not.\nذٰ لِكُمُ اللّٰهُ رَبُّكُمْ خَالِقُ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ‌ ۘ لَّاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ ‌ۚ  فَاَ نّٰى تُؤْفَكُوْنَ‏(62)\nZAA LEKUMU LAAHO RABBOKUM KHAALEQU KULLE SHAY-IN LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA FA-ALQEEHE NNAA TUFAKOONA.\nThat is God, your Lord, the Creator of everything; there is no god but He; why then are ye turned away?\nكَذٰلِكَ يُؤْفَكُ الَّذِيْنَ كَانُوْا بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ يَجْحَدُوْنَ‏(63)\nKAZAALEKA YUFAKU LAZEENA KAANOO BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE YAJHADOON.\nThus were turned away those who denied the signs of God.\nاَللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ الْاَرْضَ قَرَارًا وَّالسَّمَآءَ بِنَآءً وَّصَوَّرَكُمْ فَاَحْسَنَ صُوَرَكُمْ وَرَزَقَكُمْ مِّنَ الطَّيِّبٰتِ ؕ ذٰ لِكُمُ اللّٰهُ رَبُّكُمْ ‌ ۖۚ فَتَبٰرَكَ اللّٰهُ رَبُّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(64)\nALLAAHO LAZEE JA-A’LA LAKOMUL ARZA QARAARAWN WAS SAMAAA-A BENAAA-ANW WWASAWRAKUM FA AHSANAL SOORAKUM WARAZAQAKUM MENAL AT-TAYBAATE ZAA LEKUMU LAAHO RABBOKUM FA TABAARAKAS-MO LAAHO RABBUL A’ALAMEEN.\nGod is He Who made for you the earth to stay and the heaven a canopy, and shapened you, and made goodly your forms, and provided you with sustenance with goodly things; that is God your Lord; Hallowed is then God the Lord of the worlds.\nهُوَ الْحَىُّ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ فَادْعُوْهُ مُخْلِصِيْنَ لَهُ الدِّيْنَؕ اَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(65)\nHOWA HAYYUL LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA FAADU’OOHU MUKHLESEENA LAHUL AD-DEENA AALHAMDU LILLAAHE RABBE A’ALAMEEN.\nHe is the (Ever) Living, there is no god but He so call ye upon Him, devoting unto Him the religion; All praise is God’s, the Lord of the worlds.\nقُلْ اِنِّىْ نُهِيْتُ اَنْ اَعْبُدَ الَّذِيْنَ تَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ لَمَّا جَآءَنِىَ الْبَيِّنٰتُ مِنْ رَّبِّىْ وَاُمِرْتُ اَنْ اُسْلِمَ لِرَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(66)\nQUL INNEE NUHEETU AN HAAZEHIL BALDATIL LAZEENA TADU’OONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE LAMMAA JAAANEAAA BAYYENAATO MIN A-A’LAMO WA AN A-A’BODA AN AUSLEMA LE-RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nSay: “Verily I am forbidden to worship those whom ye call upon besides God when clear proofs have come unto me from my Lord, and I have been commanded to submit myself unto the Lord of the worlds.\nهُوَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَكُمْ مِّنْ تُرَابٍ ثُمَّ مِنْ نُّطْفَةٍ ثُمَّ مِنْ عَلَقَةٍ ثُمَّ يُخْرِجُكُمْ طِفْلًا ثُمَّ لِتَبْلُغُوْۤا اَشُدَّكُمْ ثُمَّ لِتَكُوْنُوْا شُيُوْخًا ؕ وَمِنْكُمْ مَّنْ يُّتَوَفّٰى مِنْ قَبْلُ وَلِتَبْلُغُوْۤا اَجَلًا مُّسَمًّى وَّلَعَلَّكُمْ تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(67)\nHOWA LAZEE KHALAQAKUM MIN TORAABIN SUMMA MIN NUTFATIN SUMMA MIN A’ALAQATIN SUMMA YUKHREJUKUM TEFLAN SUMMA LETABLUGHOOA AASHUDDAKUM SUMMA LE-TAKOONOO SHUYOOKHAN WA MINKUM MAN YYUTAWAFFAA MIN QABLO WALETABLUGHOOA AAJALAN AJALIM WWALAA’ALLAKUM TA’QELOON.\nHe it is Who created you from dust, then from a life-germ, then from a clot, then He bringeth you forth as a babe, then that ye may reach your full strength, then that ye may be old, and of you are those who are caused to die early and that ye may reach the appointed term, and (all this is related) that happly ye may understand.\nهُوَ الَّذِىْ يُحْىٖ وَيُمِيْتُؕ فَاِذَا قَضٰٓى اَمْرًا فَاِنَّمَا يَقُوْلُ لَهٗ كُنْ فَيَكُوْنُ‏(68)\nHOWA LAZEE YOHYEE WA YOMEET FA-EZAA QAZAA AMRAN FA-INNAMAA YAQOOLO LAHU KUN FAYAKUN.\nHe it is Who giveth life and causeth death, and when He decreeth an affair, He only sayeth unto it ‘BE’ and it IS.\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ يُجَادِلُوْنَ فِىْۤ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِؕ اَنّٰى يُصْرَفُوْنَ  ۛۚ ۙ‏(69)\nALAM TARA ELAL LAZEENA YUJAADELOONA FEE AAYAATIL LAAH ANNAA YUSRAFOONA.\nSeest thou not those who dispute about the signs of God; how they are turned away?\nالَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِالْكِتٰبِ وَبِمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا بِهٖ رُسُلَنَا ۛ  فَسَوْفَ يَعْلَمُوْنَ ۙ‏(70)\nLAZEENA KAZZABOO BE-KETAABE WA BEMAA ARSALNAA BEHI RUSULANAA FA-SAWFA YA’LAMOON.\nThose who belie the Book and what We sent Our Apostles with; then soon shall they know,\nاِذِ الْاَغْلٰلُ فِىْۤ اَعْنَاقِهِمْ وَالسَّلٰسِلُؕ يُسْحَبُوْنَۙ‏(71)\nEZIM AL-AAGHLAALU FEE AAA’NAAQEHEM WAALSSALAASELU YUSHABOONA.\nWhen the fetters shall be in their necks and the chains; they will be dragged,\nفِى الْحَمِيْمِ ۙ ثُمَّ فِى النَّارِ يُسْجَرُوْنَ‌ ۚ‏(72)\nFIL HAMEEM SUMMA FIL NAAR YUSJAROONA.\nInto the boiling water, then in the fire shall they be burned;\nثُمَّ قِيْلَ لَهُمْ اَيْنَ مَا كُنْتُمْ تُشْرِكُوْنَۙ‏(73)\nSUMMA QEELA LAHUM AYNA MAA KUNTUM TUSHREKOONA.\nThen it shall be said unto them; “Where are those whom ye used to associate (as gods),\nمِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ ؕ قَالُوْا ضَلُّوْا عَنَّا بَلْ لَّمْ نَكُنْ نَّدْعُوْا مِنْ قَبْلُ شَيْئًا ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يُضِلُّ اللّٰهُ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(74)\nMIN DOONIL LAAHE QAALOO ZALLOOA WAGH BAL LAM NAKUN NNADU’OOA MIN QABLO SHAY-ANW KAZAALEKA YOZILLO LAAHO KAAFEREEN.\nBesides God?” They shall say: “They have gone away from us, nay, we used not to call upon anything before;” Thus doth God leave the disbelievers to stray.\nذٰ لِكُمْ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَفْرَحُوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ بِغَيْرِ الْحَقِّ وَبِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَمْرَحُوْنَ‌ ۚ‏(75)\nZAA ZAALEKUM BEMAA KUNTUM TAFRAHOON FIL ARZE BEGHAYRIL HAQQE WA BEMAA KUNTUM TAMRAHOONA.\n(It will be said unto them) “This because ye exulted in the land without any right, and because ye were insolent.\nاُدْخُلُوْۤا اَبْوَابَ جَهَنَّمَ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا ۚ فَبِئْسَ مَثْوَى الْمُتَكَبِّرِيْنَ‏(76)\nAUDKHULOOA AABWAABA JAHANNAMA KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA FA MASALUL MASWAA AL-MUTAKABBEREENA.\nEnter ye the gates of Hell to abide therein.” Wretched then shall be the abode of the arrogant ones.\nفَاصْبِرْ اِنَّ وَعْدَ اللّٰهِ حَقٌّۚ فَاِمَّا نُرِيَنَّكَ بَعْضَ الَّذِىْ نَعِدُهُمْ اَوْ نَتَوَفَّيَنَّكَ فَاِلَيْنَا يُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(77)\nFAS-BIR INNAL WA’DAL LAAHE HAQQUWN FA-IMMAA NUREENNAKA YAWM LAZEE NAE’EDUHUM AW NATAWAFFAYANNAKA FA ELAYNAA YARJEO’ON.\nSo be patient thou, verily the promise of God is true; And whether We let thee see of what We threaten them with, or We cause thee to die (before that), unto Us shall they be returned.\nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا رُسُلًا مِّنْ قَبْلِكَ مِنْهُمْ مَّنْ قَصَصْنَا عَلَيْكَ وَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ لَّمْ نَقْصُصْ عَلَيْكَؕ وَمَا كَانَ لِرَسُوْلٍ اَنْ يَّاْتِىَ بِاٰيَةٍ اِلَّا بِاِذْنِ اللّٰه‌ِۚ فَاِذَا جَآءَ اَمْرُ اللّٰهِ قُضِىَ بِالْحَقِّ وَخَسِرَ هُنَالِكَ الْمُبْطِلُوْنَ‏(78)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA ROSOLAN MIN QABLEKA MINHUM MAN QASASNAA A’LAYKA WA MINHUM MAN LAM NAQSUS A’LAYK WA MAA KAANA LE-RASOOLIN AN YAATEYA BE-AAYATIL ILLAA BE-IZNIL LAAHE FA-EZAA JAAA-A AMRUL LAAHE QUZEAAA BIL-HAQQE WAKHASERA HONAALEKAB MUBTELOON.\nAnd verily sent We apostles before thee, of them there are those whom We have mentioned unto thee; and of them are those whom We have mentioned not unto thee; and it was not given to any apostle to bring a sign (miracle) save with the leave of God, but when came the behest of God, (it) was executed with truth, and those who stood on falsehood were then the losers.\nاَللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ الْاَنْعَامَ لِتَرْكَبُوْا مِنْهَا وَمِنْهَا تَاْكُلُوْنَ‏(79)\nALLAAHO LAZEE JA-A’LA LAKOMUL AL-AANA’AAMA LETARKABOOA MINHAA WA MINHAA TAAKULOONA.\nGod is He Who made for you the cattle that ye may ride on some of them, and of them ye may eat.\nوَلَكُمْ فِيْهَا مَنَافِعُ وَ لِتَبْلُغُوْا عَلَيْهَا حَاجَةً فِىْ صُدُوْرِكُمْ وَعَلَيْهَا وَعَلَى الْفُلْكِ تُحْمَلُوْنَؕ‏(80)\nWA LAKUM FEEHAA MANAAFE-O’ WA LETABLUGHOOA A’LAYHAA HAAJATAM FEE SUDOOREKUM MAKTASABAT RABBANAA WA FULKE TUHMALOONA.\nAnd for you in them are other benefits, and that ye may realize thereon the need ye cherish in your breasts; and upon them and upon the ships ye are borne.\nوَيُرِيْكُمْ اٰيٰتِهٖ ۖ  فَاَىَّ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ تُنْكِرُوْنَ‏(81)\nYOREEKUM AAYAATEHI FAAAAAA AAYAATIL LAAHE TUNKEROONA.\nAnd He showeth you His Signs; which, then, of the Signs of God will ye deny?\nاَفَلَمْ يَسِيْرُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ فَيَنْظُرُوْا كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْؕ كَانُوْۤا اَكْثَرَ مِنْهُمْ وَاَشَدَّ قُوَّةً وَّ اٰثَارًا فِى الْاَرْضِ فَمَاۤ اَغْنٰى عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(82)\nA-FALAM YASEEROO FIL ARZE FAYANZOROO KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM KAANOO AKSARAN MINHUM WA ASHADDA QUWWAH WA AAASAARAN FIL ARZE FAMAA AGHNAA A’NHUM MAA KAANOO YAKSEBOON.\nWhat! have they not travelled in the earth and seen how was the end of those before them? They were more (in number) than those and mightier in strength, and greater are their relics (of their power) in the earth, but availed them not what they were earning.\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَتْهُمْ رُسُلُهُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ فَرِحُوْا بِمَا عِنْدَهُمْ مِّنَ الْعِلْمِ وَحَاقَ بِهِمْ مَّا كَانُوْا بِهٖ يَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(83)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-AHUM JAAA-ATHUM BIL-BAYYENAATE FAREHOO BEMAA E’ENDAHUM MENAL I’LME WAHAAQA BEHIM MAA KAANOO BEHI YASTAHZEOON.\nAnd when came unto them their apostles with clear proofs (of their truthfulness), exulted they in what they had with them of knowledge, but encompassed them that which they were wont to scoff.\nفَلَمَّا رَاَوْا بَاْسَنَا قَالُوْۤا اٰمَنَّا بِاللّٰهِ وَحْدَهٗ وَكَفَرْنَا بِمَا كُنَّا بِهٖ مُشْرِكِيْنَ‏(84)\nFALAMMAA RA-AW BAASANAA QAALOO AAMANNAA BIL-LAAHE WAHDAH WAKAFARNAA BEMAA KUNNAA BEHI MUSHREKEENA.\nBut when they beheld Our punishment said they: “We believe in God alone and we deny what we used to associate with Him.\nفَلَمْ يَكُ يَنْفَعُهُمْ اِيْمَانُهُمْ لَمَّا رَاَوْا بَاْسَنَا ؕ سُنَّتَ اللّٰهِ الَّتِىْ قَدْ خَلَتْ فِىْ عِبَادِهٖ‌ۚ وَخَسِرَ هُنَالِكَ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ‏(85)\nFALAM YAKU YANFAU’UHUM AEEMAANUHUM LAMMAA RA-AW BAASANAA SUNNATA LAAHE LATEE QAD KHALAT FEE E’BAADEHI WAKHASERA HONAALEKAB KAAFEROON.\nBut shall not benefit them their faith when they had beheld Our punishment; (such is) the procedure of God which hath indeed been in use concerning His servants; and then the disbelievers have lost.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Mo’min (The Believer) Or Surah Ghaafir\nThis is a ‘Makki’ Surah and it has 85 verses. When a person recites this Surah then the souls of all the Prophet (a.s.), the truthful people and the believers send salutations to him and pray for his forgiveness. Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that whoever recites this Surah once in every three days, his sins will be forgiven and he will become a God-fearing person.\nIt is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that if this Surah is written and kept in a garden or farm, then the plants or crops will become more fruit bearing and green. If kept in a business premises then business will prosper and more profit will be gained. Keeping this Surah as a talisman works as a cure for wounds and scars. This Surah is also a remedy for heart problems, dizziness and nausea."
}
